{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1476214-how-does-glamour-stay-hidden","id":1476214,"title":"How does Glamour stay hidden?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-03-11T10:08:05-08:00","id":1476214,"title":"How does Glamour stay hidden?","content":"I know Changelings, Tokens, and even True Fae generate Masks to keep their true selves hidden, but what about the other effects of Glamour such as Hobgoblins or Contract use? <br /> <br /> Can a normal individual stumble upon a rare Hobgoblin that wanders outside the Hedge and perceive it for what it is?<br /> <br /> How does the existence of this wonderful world stay secret?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9255-docsteve2020","name":"DocSteve2020","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-11T11:03:41-08:00","id":1476217,"title":"","content":"Hobgoblins wither and ache when they leave the Hedge, so they don't do it often.<br /> The effects of Contracts aren't hidden. Using supernatural powers draws attention, though, and some changelings grow paranoid of what might draw the attention of the Wild Hunt. Using them openly in front of mortals a lot is also a great way to invite Clarity attacks as people try to come up with alternate explanations.<br /> <br /> In the Chronicles of Darkness, the supernatural <i>doesn't</i> stay perfectly hidden. The five questions asked of every mortal character to calibrate their Integrity include &quot;what encounter with the supernatural have you had and convinced yourself didn't happen?&quot; The main consistent reasons society at large hasn't exposed the supernatural are the collective fear of the unknown (what if it's real <i>and saying it's real draws its attention?)</i> and the sense of isolating self-doubt that others haven't seen what you've seen (especially when you're not perfectly sure you saw it).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}